Problem: The parabola $y=x^2+2$ and the hyperbola $y^2-16x^2=16$ intersect at four points $(x_i,y_j)$ for $1\le i\le 4$ and $1\le j\le 4.$ If $\sum_{i=1}^4 x_i$ can be expressed as $\frac{a}{b},$ where $a$ and $b$ are coprime positive integers, find $a+b.$

[asy]
size(150);
real b=0.1;
real f(real x) {return x^2+2;}
real g(real x) {return 4x;}
real h(real x) {return -4x;}
draw(reflect((0,0),(1/2,sqrt(5)/2))*graph(f,-sqrt(5)-b,sqrt(5)+b),red);
draw(graph(g,-b,1/b),blue);
draw(graph(h,-b,1/b),blue);
limits(-1,-5,5,10,black+linewidth(.75));
[/asy]

